.TH NYX-ARPSPOOF 8 "2025" "NYX Framework" "NYX Phobos Tools"
.SH NAME
nyx-arpspoof \- ARP cache poisoning tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nyx-arpspoof
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nyx-arpspoof
performs ARP cache poisoning on a local network segment. It sends
forged ARP reply packets to a target host, causing it to associate
the attacker's MAC address with another IP (typically the default
gateway). This redirects traffic through the attacker's machine,
enabling man-in-the-middle analysis.
.PP
When launched, it enters an interactive shell with line editing,
tab completion, and command history. Type
.B help
for available commands.
.PP
The tool supports bidirectional poisoning (both the target and the
gateway) and automatically restores the original ARP mappings on
exit (Ctrl-C / SIGINT / SIGTERM).
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.BI start " -i iface -t target -s spoof" " [-b]" " [-n sec]"
Start ARP poisoning. Options:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-i " iface" "\fR, \fP" \-\-interface " iface"
Network interface (required).
.TP
.BI \-t " ip" "\fR, \fP" \-\-target " ip"
Victim IP address (required).
.TP
.BI \-s " ip" "\fR, \fP" \-\-spoof " ip"
IP to impersonate, e.g. the gateway (required).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bidirectional
Poison both directions.
.TP
.BI \-n " sec" "\fR, \fP" \-\-interval " sec"
Seconds between ARP packets. Default is 1.
.RE
.TP
.B list
List available network interfaces.
.TP
.B help
Show available commands and usage.
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
sudo nyx-arpspoof
arpspoof> start -i eth0 -t 192.168.1.5 -s 192.168.1.1
arpspoof> start -i wlan0 -t 10.0.0.5 -s 10.0.0.1 -b -n 2
arpspoof> list
arpspoof> exit
.fi
.SH NOTES
This tool requires root privileges (raw packet sockets). When launched
without root from a terminal, it will attempt to re-execute itself
with sudo.
.PP
ARP tables are automatically restored when the tool receives
SIGINT (Ctrl-C) or SIGTERM.
